Hmm. PDF is an open format; you can create it with many open source
tools as well! And it has some quite nice features:

- central place (Adobe) to get a halfways-decent reader which even
exquisitely dumb users know.
- can store document structure (convenience, accessibility, handhelds..)
- rudimentary but sufficient presentation and form functions

In fact I wouldn't know what would be more convenient than PDF if I had
a presentation with complex math formulae or one that I'd like to be
portable... what would you use?

